---
import:
  - undying-tide-base
requires:
  - ocean
description: Depths - gene fragments, the Rift, ever deeper levels, the darkness, pulses and plankton.
---

***implementation reqs***

- :Implementation: draws every :Wave: of a :Level: from a generator of `src/game/sim/random.ts` seeded from the :RunSeed: and the :Depth:, apart from the one the :Level: layouts are drawn from, so waves change no other draw of the :Run:.

***functional specs***

- Each :Level: holds `4 + :Depth:` :GeneFragment: items, placed from the :RunSeed:, which the :Jellyfish: collects by touching them.
  - Each :GeneFragment: lies at least 40 px inside every edge, at least 120 px from the :Jellyfish: start `(640, 360)`, and at least 80 px from every other :GeneFragment:.
  - A :GeneFragment: is collected when its circle overlaps the :Jellyfish: circle, and then disappears.
  - :Hud: shows `Depth <n>` and `Fragments <collected>/<total>`.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `depth`, and `fragments`, the list of the :Level:'s :GeneFragment: items, each with `x`, `y` and `collected`.
  - The same :RunSeed: places the :GeneFragment: items of each :Depth: at the same positions.

- Each :Level: has one :Rift:, which opens once every :GeneFragment: of the :Level: is collected; swimming into an open :Rift: takes the :Run: to the next :Depth:.
  - The :Rift: lies, from the :RunSeed:, at least 60 px inside every edge, at least 200 px from `(640, 360)`, and at least 60 px from every :GeneFragment:.
  - A closed :Rift: is drawn in the palette's closed-rift colour and does nothing when touched; an open one glows in the open-rift colour.
  - The :Jellyfish: enters an open :Rift: when its circle overlaps the :Rift: circle.
  - The next :Level: starts with its :Depth: one higher, a new layout from the :RunSeed:, and the :Jellyfish: at rest at `(640, 360)`, upright, its :Heading: 0.
  - :Hud: shows `Rift open` while the :Rift: is open.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `rift`, with `x`, `y` and `open`.

- Each :Level: starts its :Pulses: at `max(20, 65 - 5 × :Depth:)` - 60 at :Depth: 1 - and runs them down by 1 a second while a direction key is held and by 0.5 a second otherwise.
  - Opposite direction keys held together count as no direction held.
  - :Pulses: never runs down while the :Run: is paused.
  - When :Pulses: reaches 0, it stays at 0 until it is refilled.
  - :Hud: shows `Pulses <n>`, :Pulses: rounded up, beside a bar of :Pulses: against its start for the :Level:, in the palette's pulse-bar colour, and in its danger colour at 10 or fewer.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `pulses` (unrounded), `pulsesStart`, `ended` (boolean) and `endReason` (`null` until the :RunEnd:).
  - P and Escape do nothing after the :RunEnd:.

- Each :Level: holds 3 :PlanktonCloud: items, placed from the :RunSeed:; touching one adds 15 to :Pulses:, up to its start for the :Level:, and uses the :PlanktonCloud: up.
  - Each :PlanktonCloud: lies at least 40 px inside every edge, at least 100 px from `(640, 360)`, and at least 60 px from the :Rift:, every :GeneFragment: and every other :PlanktonCloud:.
  - A :PlanktonCloud: is touched when its circle overlaps the :Jellyfish: circle.
  - A used-up :PlanktonCloud: disappears, and is used up even when :Pulses: is already at its start.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `plankton`, the list of :PlanktonCloud: items, each with `x`, `y` and `used`.

- Each :Level: is drawn darker the deeper it is: its water takes the palette gradient of its :Depth: band, and only what lies within the :Glow: is seen.
  - The :Glow: radius is `max(160, 1469 × 0.88^(:Depth: - 1))` px - 1469 px, the whole screen, at :Depth: 1.
  - Outside the :Glow:, the :Level: is covered by the palette's darkness overlay, fully opaque from 40 px beyond its edge and fading in over those 40 px.
  - An open :Rift: stays visible through the darkness.
  - :Hud: is drawn above the darkness.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `glowRadius`.

- From :Depth: 2, :Wave: items rise in each :Level:, one at a time; each warns for 1 s, pushing nothing, then pushes for 3 s the :Jellyfish: along its direction at its strength while their circles overlap.
  - The first :Wave: of a :Level: rises 4 to 8 s after the :Level: starts, and each next one 6 to 12 s after the one before it ends.
  - Each :Wave: draws its wait, centre, radius, direction and strength from the :RunSeed:: its centre anywhere in the :Level:, its radius 150 to 350 px, its direction 0 to 360°, its strength 80 to 200 px/s.
  - These ranges are the same at every :Depth: from 2 on.
  - Its push rises from 0 to its strength over the first 0.5 s of the 3 s and falls back to 0 over the last 0.5 s.
  - The push moves the :Jellyfish: on top of its own swimming and leaves its `vx`, `vy` and :Heading: unchanged; its centre still stays at least 24 px inside each edge.
  - Gene fragments, plankton clouds and the :Rift: are never moved.
  - A :Wave: takes no :Hearts: and no :Pulses:.
  - A :Wave: and its timers stand still while the :Run: is paused and after the :RunEnd:; a :Wave: still running when the :Level: ends is gone in the next :Level:.
  - At :Depth: 1 no :Wave: rises.
  - The same :RunSeed: gives each :Depth: the same :Wave: items at the same ticks.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `wave`, `null` while none is up, else with `x`, `y`, `radius`, `direction`, `strength`, `phase` (`warning` or `pushing`) and `timeLeft` (seconds left in that phase).
